    "title": "How do you handle concurrency conflicts in EF Core?",
    "category": "3. EF Core Advanced",
    "language": "csharp",
    "explanation": "When a concurrency conflict occurs, EF Core throws a `DbUpdateConcurrencyException`. You catch this exception and typically use one of three resolution strategies:\n1. **Client Wins:** The user's submitted values forcefully overwrite the database values.\n2. **Database Wins:** The user's changes are discarded, and the new database values are shown to the user.\n3. **Custom Merge:** The application attempts to intelligently merge the changes, or asks the user what to do.",
    "example": "Handling a \"Database Wins\" scenario.",
    "code": "try {\n    await _context.SaveChangesAsync();\n}\ncatch (DbUpdateConcurrencyException ex) {\n    foreach (var entry in ex.Entries) {\n        // Overwrite the tracked entity with the fresh database values\n        var databaseValues = await entry.GetDatabaseValuesAsync();\n        entry.OriginalValues.SetValues(databaseValues);\n    }\n    // You could retry the save here, or throw an error back to the UI\n    throw new Exception(\"Data was modified by someone else.\");\n}",
