    "title": "What is the difference between First() and FirstOrDefault()?",
    "category": "5. LINQ Operators",
    "language": "csharp",
    "explanation": "Both methods retrieve the very first element of a sequence (optionally matching a predicate condition).\n- **`First()`:** Expects that at least one element exists. If the collection is empty (or no elements match the predicate), it **throws an `InvalidOperationException`**.\n- **`FirstOrDefault()`:** Is safe. If the collection is empty, it returns the default value for the type (which is `null` for reference types like classes, and `0` for numeric types).",
