    "category": "9. Real-Project Scenarios",
    "language": "csharp",
    "explanation": "When EF Core loads an entity normally, it takes the data from the database, creates a C# object, and then creates a duplicate 'snapshot' of that object inside the `ChangeTracker` memory space. It maintains a constant reference to monitor it for modifications.\n`AsNoTracking()` tells EF Core to skip the Change Tracker entirely. \nIt is faster because it saves the CPU cycles required to set up the tracking, and it uses roughly half the RAM because it doesn't need to hold the snapshot.",
